NO WARRANTY -- AND WHY THAT MATTERS FOR THIS PARTICULAR TOOL
    Sections 7 and 8 of the LICENSE disclaim all warranties and liability.
    That is standard, and it is worth reading rather than skipping here.

    Netwise reports on the security of network device configurations. A
    clean result from Netwise is not a statement that a network is secure.
    The tool checks specific properties, against configurations it can
    parse, using policy assertions someone wrote. It distinguishes "we
    checked and found nothing" from "we could not check" -- see F-4 in
    docs/finding-format.md -- precisely because conflating the two would be
    the most dangerous thing it could do.

    Nothing in this software should be treated as a security audit, and no
    contributor accepts liability for decisions made on the basis of its
    output.
